# Supabase — Project Settings > API keys.
# Both are server-only: no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so Next never ships them to
# the browser. The page talks to Supabase only from server code.
# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in.
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co

# The `sb_secret_...` key ("secret", formerly service_role). Never commit it,
# never expose it to the browser. In production set it as a deployment secret.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Public production origin used for canonical URLs and the sitemap.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://boatuneet.com
# Listing Lab: configure ONE server-only search provider locally and in Vercel.
# Tavily takes precedence when both are set. Never use NEXT_PUBLIC_ for secrets.
# A free account is sufficient for a small pilot. Keep paid overages disabled.
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# BRAVE_SEARCH_API_KEY=

# Meta Lead Ads webhook (/api/meta/leads). All server-only.
# META_VERIFY_TOKEN: any random string, pasted into the Meta app's webhook setup.
# META_APP_SECRET: Meta app > Settings > Basic. Verifies X-Hub-Signature-256.
# META_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN: long-lived Page token with leads_retrieval + pages_manage_ads.
# META_VERIFY_TOKEN=
# META_APP_SECRET=
# META_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional Meta Pixel. Loads only after the visitor accepts advertising cookies.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=
